{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"western-terrazzo-perch","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered while implementing e9d5-c850-d505-4a5a (typed reconciler mutation\npayload contracts, ADR 0107). Two producers construct (outbound, update)\nMutation payloads with different shapes:\n\n- differ.py's older `_compute_mutations_emit_both` path emits a flat,\n  unwrapped `changed` dict directly as `Mutation.payload`.\n- outbound_pass.py / binding_walk.py wrap the same information as\n  `{\"changed_fields\": {...}, \"comments\": [...], \"labels\": [...], \"links\": [...]}`.\n\nADR 0107's typed `OutboundUpdatePayload` contract standardizes on the wrapped\nshape (`changed_fields`); the flat legacy shape from differ.py's older path\nwould fail typed validation today. This is a pre-existing inconsistency,\nNOT introduced by e9d5 — e9d5 only documents it (see the corpus README and\ne9d5's ticket comment recording approved intentional deltas and does not\nreconcile it, since producer rewiring is ADR 0107's deferred Cut step and\nout of e9d5's own scope (AC7).\n\nSuggested follow-up: decide (a) which shape is canonical going forward, and\n(b) migrate differ.py's  to emit the wrapped\n shape so both producers agree before any producer is\nrewired to construct  directly (that Cut step is a\nseparate, later ticket).\nEOF\n)","id":"162e-57c3-f7d4-4457","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Reconcile dual outbound-update payload shapes (differ.py flat vs outbound_pass.py wrapped)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788109201597861001,"uuid":"be1f7bba-f383-4e27-bb3d-502e892cba00"}